#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720223 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eaa2d5a3-aa18-5cf4-91d3-9f5bcbe727d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eaa2d5a3-aa18-5cf4-91d3-9f5bcbe727d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720224} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c23a9f2-60f9-5f99-b97b-f53aac0935a5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720213}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "db748b7e-d095-5e09-af17-f5087dfa3134" :question/problem "Suppose $\\mathbf{b}\\times \\mathbf{c}=\\langle 3,2,0\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 0,-1,-3\\rangle$. Find $\\mathbf{b}\\cdot\\bigl(\\mathbf{a}\\times \\mathbf{c}\\bigr)$.\n\n$\\mathbf{b}\\cdot\\bigl(\\mathbf{a}\\times \\mathbf{c}\\bigr)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First take the dot product with the remaining vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{a}\\cdot\\bigl(\\mathbf{b}\\times \\mathbf{c}\\bigr)&=\\langle 0,-1,-3\\rangle\\cdot \\langle 3,2,0\\rangle \\\\\n&=(0)\\cdot (3)+(-1)\\cdot (2)+(-3)\\cdot (0) \\\\\n&=-2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSwap $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$; one swap reverses the sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{b}\\cdot\\bigl(\\mathbf{a}\\times \\mathbf{c}\\bigr)&=2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe requested scalar is $2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720338 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation." :answer/id #uuid "3d369dd0-9d68-5c2f-83e7-161494874fb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(3 t^{2}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720341} {:answer/feedback "Include the speed $\\sqrt{1+(y\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t))^2}$." :answer/id #uuid "58d19996-d5f1-53bf-9bb7-40990e17f3ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left(t^{4}\\right)\\,1\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720344} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. Include the speed $\\sqrt{1+(y\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t))^2}$." :answer/id #uuid "99e20784-2f54-58f7-a5c5-33fdca666252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,1\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720359} {:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "c6251dbe-177f-5004-b27f-561a66bdc88b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left(t^{4}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(3 t^{2}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720361} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. Include the speed $\\sqrt{1+(y\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t))^2}$." :answer/id #uuid "cff0a842-04f7-52ae-829f-b55a24151f01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left(t^{7}\\right)\\,1\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "c6251dbe-177f-5004-b27f-561a66bdc88b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left(t^{4}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(3 t^{2}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720361} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3a7d462-2cbe-5a6b-bf48-e9905ff6194d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "30268687-c5b9-59fc-beaf-a8a0bacc2204" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the section of $y=x^{3}$ for $-1\\le x\\le 2$.\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nusing $x=t$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "Set $x=t$. Parametrize the curve by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,t^{3}\\rangle,\\qquad -1\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinates and take the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle 1,3 t^{2}\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{1+\\left(3 t^{2}\\right)^2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates into the scalar function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=t \\left(t^{3}\\right)\\\\\n&=t^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the scalar by the speed and use the parameter bounds:\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{-1}^{2} f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nThus the required setup is\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left(t^{4}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(3 t^{2}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720350 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. The speed is a square root of the sum of squared coordinate derivatives." :answer/id #uuid "3b38f325-46e1-59f4-9618-7c17eefaa973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(- 2 t^{4}\\right)\\,\\left(1+\\left(- \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\right)^2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720339} {:answer/feedback "The speed is a square root of the sum of squared coordinate derivatives." :answer/id #uuid "3c57b28f-dfb7-591f-8ae7-1461a71b9e3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(- 2 t^{2}\\right)\\,\\left(1+\\left(- \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\right)^2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720340} {:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "75e1fd21-a7b0-54f6-914c-f70c08ccc592" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(- 2 t^{2}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(- \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720349} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation." :answer/id #uuid "95a87577-af60-5342-9b42-35b2039e699e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(- 2 t^{3}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(- \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720356} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. The speed is a square root of the sum of squared coordinate derivatives." :answer/id #uuid "d291feaa-0a6b-5640-970b-e27cb025c86f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(- 2 t^{3}\\right)\\,\\left(1+\\left(- \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\right)^2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "75e1fd21-a7b0-54f6-914c-f70c08ccc592" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(- 2 t^{2}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(- \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720349} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a2aa7ac-41e7-5f91-86c4-31e917e6dfa4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7cf692c7-198c-5ca9-a401-bf72fb6876a7" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the section of $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ for $1\\le x\\le 3$.\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(- 2 x^{3} y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nusing $x=t$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "Set $x=t$. Parametrize the curve by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,\\frac{1}{t}\\rangle,\\qquad 1\\le t\\le 3.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinates and take the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle 1,- \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{1+\\left(- \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\right)^2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates into the scalar function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=- 2 t^{3} \\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right)\\\\\n&=- 2 t^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the scalar by the speed and use the parameter bounds:\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{1}^{3} f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nThus the required setup is\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{3}\\left(- 2 t^{2}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(- \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720351 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. Include the speed $\\sqrt{1+(y\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t))^2}$." :answer/id #uuid "0b3a4fac-d3bb-5697-8029-693a3e212c14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(2 e^{t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,1\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720335} {:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "4d71471b-4674-5a4e-99aa-3a2ba9410a26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(2 e^{t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(2 e^{t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720343} {:answer/feedback "Include the speed $\\sqrt{1+(y\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t))^2}$." :answer/id #uuid "63af26ff-9eae-5565-b6fd-fa0c024f0ce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(2 e^{t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,1\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720346} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation." :answer/id #uuid "8e3abaed-d985-5377-8a38-45dc8e55de86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(2 e^{t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720352} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. Include the speed $\\sqrt{1+(y\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t))^2}$." :answer/id #uuid "d074b37e-9332-5304-bcff-6fb04978ea72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,1\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "4d71471b-4674-5a4e-99aa-3a2ba9410a26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(2 e^{t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(2 e^{t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720343} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cfeba7f-f2b7-590b-9165-20ba3f7988b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720336}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d818492-ef87-5a5e-9d9a-04fd5ac3c65b" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the section of $y=2 e^{x}$ for $1\\le x\\le 2$.\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(y \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nusing $x=t$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "Set $x=t$. Parametrize the curve by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,2 e^{t}\\rangle,\\qquad 1\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinates and take the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle 1,2 e^{t}\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{1+\\left(2 e^{t}\\right)^2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates into the scalar function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\left(2 e^{t}\\right) \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\\\\n&=2 e^{t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the scalar by the speed and use the parameter bounds:\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{1}^{2} f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nThus the required setup is\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(2 e^{t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(2 e^{t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720355 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. The speed is a square root of the sum of squared coordinate derivatives." :answer/id #