 and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "5ec4b9d6-72cb-5a58-9369-0508ad8f98a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left(\\left(3 t + 1\\right) e^{t}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(3\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720345} :answer-field/id #uuid "71529b37-61a6-5ee5-a4f3-ccc36e16302c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "93335b1e-e511-5409-ba55-633670837cd5" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the section of $y=3 x + 1$ for $-1\\le x\\le 2$.\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(y e^{x}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nusing $x=t$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "Set $x=t$. Parametrize the curve by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,3 t + 1\\rangle,\\qquad -1\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinates and take the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle 1,3\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{1+\\left(3\\right)^2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates into the scalar function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\left(3 t + 1\\right) e^{t}\\\\\n&=\\left(3 t + 1\\right) e^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the scalar by the speed and use the parameter bounds:\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{-1}^{2} f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nThus the required setup is\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left(\\left(3 t + 1\\right) e^{t}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(3\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720367 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id 