ositive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "70d31a18-2de3-5adb-92be-e458e14c4b15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-2}^{-1}\\left(t^{3} + t + \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 1 \\right)}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(\\frac{2 t}{t^{2} + 1}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720378} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fb23117-4026-50a3-aa5e-c9d5ac778484" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8a8f5ae1-ca35-5385-acc3-098740e05b74" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the section of $y=\\ln{\\left(x^{2} + 1 \\right)}$ with $x<0$ between its intersections with the horizontal lines $y=\\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}$ and $y=\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}$.\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(x e^{y} + y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nusing $x=t$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "First solve the intersection equations on the specified branch:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln(x^{2} + 1)=\\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}&\\implies x^{2} + 1=5\\implies x=-2\\\\\n\\ln(x^{2} + 1)=\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}&\\implies x^{2} + 1=2\\implies x=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet $x=t$. Parametrize the curve by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,\\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 1 \\right)}\\rangle,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le -1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinates and take the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle 1,\\frac{2 t}{t^{2} + 1}\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{1+\\left(\\frac{2 t}{t^{2} + 1}\\right)^2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates into the scalar function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=t e^{\\left(\\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 1 \\right)}\\right)} + \\left(\\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 1 \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=t^{3} + t + \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 1 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $e^{\\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 1 \\right)}}=t^{2} + 1$ because the logarithm argument is positive on the interval.\n\nMultiply the scalar by the speed and use the parameter bounds:\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{-2}^{-1} f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nThus the required setup is\n\n$$\n\\int_{-2}^{-1}\\left(t^{3} + t + \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 1 \\right)}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(\\frac{2 t}{t^{2} + 1}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720387 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. Include the speed $\\sqrt{1+(y\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t))^2}$. The parameter is $t=x$; horizontal levels are $y$-values, not parameter limits." :answer/id #uuid "080c0fd2-ba17-51d9-b41f-8931293288ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}^{\\ln{\\left(18 \\right)}}\\left(2 t^{3} + 4 t + \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\,1\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720371} {:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "4bcc8649-2d22-5d9b-a7d0-a786a33e2a94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{4}\\left(2 t^{3} + 4 t + 2 \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(\\frac{2 t}{t^{2} + 2}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720376} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. Include the speed $\\sqrt{1+(y\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t))^2}$. The parameter is $t=x$; horizontal levels are $y$-values, not parameter limits." :answer/id #uuid "71498b74-8039-541c-a47b-5b461faf2d14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}}^{\\ln{\\left(18 \\right)}}\\left(2 t^{3} + 4 t - 2 \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\,1\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720379} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation." :answer/id #uuid "afbf68f1-0773-5df3-9446-2106134aba11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{4}\\left(2 t^{3} + 4 t + \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(\\frac{2 t}{t^{2} + 2}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720389} {:answer/feedback "Include the speed $\\sqrt{1+(y\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t))^2}$." :answer/id #uuid "e2a3e6c6-823d-53e4-bb9c-c135313d2fef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{4}\\left(2 t^{3} + 4 t + 2 \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\,1\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "4bcc8649-2d22-5d9b-a7d0-a786a33e2a94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{4}\\left(2 t^{3} + 4 t + 2 \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(\\frac{2 t}{t^{2} + 2}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720376} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffef2526-1f50-57b1-a194-061110df31a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720398}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a5c265f6-66ae-518f-8377-83fba9dfedf4" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the section of $y=\\ln{\\left(x^{2} + 2 \\right)}$ with $x>0$ between its intersections with the horizontal lines $y=\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}$ and $y=\\ln{\\left(18 \\right)}$.\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(2 x e^{y} + 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nusing $x=t$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "First solve the intersection equations on the specified branch:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln(x^{2} + 2)=\\ln{\\left(3 \\right)}&\\implies x^{2} + 2=3\\implies x=1\\\\\n\\ln(x^{2} + 2)=\\ln{\\left(18 \\right)}&\\implies x^{2} + 2=18\\implies x=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet $x=t$. Parametrize the curve by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,\\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\rangle,\\qquad 1\\le t\\le 4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinates and take the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle 1,\\frac{2 t}{t^{2} + 2}\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{1+\\left(\\frac{2 t}{t^{2} + 2}\\right)^2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates into the scalar function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=2 t e^{\\left(\\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\right)} + 2 \\left(\\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=2 t^{3} + 4 t + 2 \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $e^{\\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}}=t^{2} + 2$ because the logarithm argument is positive on the interval.\n\nMultiply the scalar by the speed and use the parameter bounds:\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{1}^{4} f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nThus the required setup is\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{4}\\left(2 t^{3} + 4 t + 2 \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(\\frac{2 t}{t^{2} + 2}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720394 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Include the speed $\\sqrt{1+(y\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t))^2}$." :answer/id #uuid "2b0ef6b5-56a0-5999-b303-904b618b548d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{2}^{4}\\left(- t^{3} - 2 t + \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\,1\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720373} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. Include the speed $\\sqrt{1+(y\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t))^2}$. The parameter is $t=x$; horizontal levels are $y$-values, not parameter limits." :answer/id #uuid "919d5671-d6fb-5a37-b13e-c482ef37fb14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\ln{\\left(6 \\right)}}^{\\ln{\\left(18 \\right)}}\\left(- t^{3} - 2 t - 2 \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\,1\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720384} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation." :answer/id #uuid "9216c699-d681-5c1a-897c-b269bb309190" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{2}^{4}\\left(- t^{3} - 2 t + 2 \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(\\frac{2 t}{t^{2} + 2}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720385} {:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "c74e979d-a881-5e7a-80c4-d16de66fec9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{2}^{4}\\left(- t^{3} - 2 t + \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(\\frac{2 t}{t^{2} + 2}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720390} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. Include the speed $\\sqrt{1+(y\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t))^2}$. The parameter is $t=x$; horizontal levels are $y$-values, not parameter limits." :answer/id #uuid "d0051372-450b-50b3-9f63-3715fd0b0c8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\ln{\\left(6 \\right)}}^{\\ln{\\left(18 \\right)}}\\left(- t^{3} - 2 t + 2 \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\,1\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "c74e979d-a881-5e7a-80c4-d16de66fec9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{2}^{4}\\left(- t^{3} - 2 t + \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(\\frac{2 t}{t^{2} + 2}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720390} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5347cb4-356b-56c9-ab68-c3dfa7a0f621" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720393}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d6391a5d-141d-5543-a2c7-b930a2a3a808" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the section of $y=\\ln{\\left(x^{2} + 2 \\right)}$ with $x>0$ between its intersections with the horizontal lines $y=\\ln{\\left(6 \\right)}$ and $y=\\ln{\\left(18 \\right)}$.\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(- x e^{y} + y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nusing $x=t$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "First solve the intersection equations on the specified branch:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln(x^{2} + 2)=\\ln{\\left(6 \\right)}&\\implies x^{2} + 2=6\\implies x=2\\\\\n\\ln(x^{2} + 2)=\\ln{\\left(18 \\right)}&\\implies x^{2} + 2=18\\implies x=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet $x=t$. Parametrize the curve by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,\\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\rangle,\\qquad 2\\le t\\le 4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinates and take the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle 1,\\frac{2 t}{t^{2} + 2}\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{1+\\left(\\frac{2 t}{t^{2} + 2}\\right)^2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates into the scalar function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=- t e^{\\left(\\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\right)} + \\left(\\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&=- t^{3} - 2 t + \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $e^{\\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}}=t^{2} + 2$ because the logarithm argument is positive on the interval.\n\nMultiply the scalar by the speed and use the parameter bounds:\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{2}^{4} f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nThus the required setup is\n\n$$\n\\int_{2}^{4}\\left(- t^{3} - 2 t + \\ln{\\left(t^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(\\frac{2 t}{t^{2} + 2}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720402 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. Include the speed $\\sqrt{1+(y\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t))^2}$. The parameter is $t=x$; horizontal levels are $y$-values, not parameter limits." :answer/id #uuid "759cd1eb-9932-5a5a-9637-d9b739f33a6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{6}^{8}\\left(e^{t}\\right)\\,1\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720406} {:answer/feedback "Include the speed $\\sqrt{1+(y\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t))^2}$." :answer/id #uuid "7aa38d40-e636-5cae-9258-1be3b2c8ccbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{2}^{3}\\left(2 \\left(t + 1\\right) e^{t}\\right)\\,1\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720407} {:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "885f2628-224d-5c72-bba5-db7f3bcb5966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{2}^{3}\\left(2 \\left(t + 1\\right) e^{t}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(2\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720411} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation." :answer/id #uuid "8b568d0b-b414-56f4-b3d2-6be306b37dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{2}^{3}\\left(e^{t}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(2\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720412} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. Include the speed $\\sqrt{1+(y\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t))^2}$. The parameter is $t=x$; horizontal levels are $y$-values, not parameter limits." :answer/id #uuid "910381fb-cab4-5610-a3ba-127950434455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{6}^{8}\\left(\\left(2 t + 2\\right) e^{2 t + 2}\\right)\\,1\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "885f2628-224d-5c72-bba5-db7f3bcb5966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{2}^{3}\\left(2 \\left(t + 1\\right) e^{t}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(2\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720411} :answer-field/id #uuid "01404010-59f8-59ea-b1ce-071c5763180c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720399}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2849cd87-a124-5767-b272-a9aa638d541d" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the section of $y=2 x + 2$ between its intersections with the horizontal lines $y=6$ and $y=8$.\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(y e^{x}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nusing $x=t$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "First solve the intersection equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 x + 2=6&\\implies x=2\\\\\n2 x + 2=8&\\implies x=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet $x=t$. Parametrize the curve by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,2 t + 2\\rangle,\\qquad 2\\le t\\le 3.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinates and take the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle 1,2\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{1+\\left(2\\right)^2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates into the scalar function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\left(2 t + 2\\right) e^{t}\\\\\n&=2 \\left(t + 1\\right) e^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the scalar by the speed and use the parameter bounds:\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{2}^{3} f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nThus the required setup is\n\n$$\n\\int_{2}^{3}\\left(2 \\left(t + 1\\right) e^{t}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(2\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720403 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. The speed is a square root of the sum of squared coordinate derivatives. The parameter is $t=x$; horizontal levels are $y$-values, not parameter limits." :answer/id #uuid "1e891d63-b6e8-5eaf-b968-9aabba59e604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{2}^{2 e}\\left(t^{2}\\right)\\,\\left(1+\\left(2 e^{t}\\right)^2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720400} {:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "8f27dc4b-b06e-5aab-87b4-13ae9a7f0870" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(2 t e^{t}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(2 e^{t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720413} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. The speed is a square root of the sum of squared coordinate derivatives. The parameter is $t=x$; horizontal levels are $y$-values, not parameter limits." :answer/id #uuid "9bb0367c-162e-502b-9833-b3e1fc9ef30d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{2}^{2 e}\\left(2 e^{t}\\right)\\,\\left(1+\\left(2 e^{t}\\right)^2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720415} {:answer/feedback "The speed is a square root of the sum of squared coordinate derivatives." :answer/id #uuid "ad2751ad-298a-57ad-ac49-b5e4e31e1a60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(2 t e^{t}\\right)\\,\\left(1+\\left(2 e^{t}\\right)^2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720419} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation." :answer/id #uuid "de382513-f326-52d2-af8f-f938a2e90383" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(2 e^{t}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(2 e^{t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "8f27dc4b-b06e-5aab-87b4-13ae9a7f0870" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(2 t e^{t}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(2 e^{t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720413} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5faccbb-e1df-5091-99cf-fcdacd79f5d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "30b83d82-6b79-5abe-a3dc-0fbc1a0b302c" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the section of $y=2 e^{x}$ between its intersections with the horizontal lines $y=2$ and $y=2 e$.\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(x y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nusing $x=t$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "First solve the intersection equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 e^{x}=2&\\implies x=0\\\\\n2 e^{x}=2 e&\\implies x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet $x=t$. Parametrize the curve by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,2 e^{t}\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinates and take the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle 1,2 e^{t}\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{1+\\left(2 e^{t}\\right)^2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates into the scalar function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=t \\left(2 e^{t}\\right)\\\\\n&=2 t e^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the scalar by the speed and use the parameter bounds:\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{0}^{1} f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nThus the required setup is\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(2 t e^{t}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(2 e^{t}\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720404 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. The speed is a square root of the sum of squared coordinate derivatives. The parameter is $t=x$; horizontal levels are $y$-values, not parameter limits." :answer/id #uuid "223ead85-4180-58e3-845a-8f84ef6fcb11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{16}\\left(- 2 t^{4}\\right)\\,\\left(1+\\left(2 t\\right)^2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720401} {:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "a565f977-b638-5c4e-9f5b-978e41f9e805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-4}^{-1}\\left(- 2 t^{2}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(2 t\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720418} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation." :answer/id #uuid "c5314c83-07dc-5025-8950-bf396e640d15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-4}^{-1}\\left(- 2 t^{4}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(2 t\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720421} {:answer/feedback "The speed is a square root of the sum of squared coordinate derivatives." :answer/id #uuid "d1bebb1a-718e-5def-a41d-4fdd45b03464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-4}^{-1}\\left(- 2 t^{2}\\right)\\,\\left(1+\\left(2 t\\right)^2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720423} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. The speed is a square root of the sum of squared coordinate derivatives. The parameter is $t=x$; horizontal levels are $y$-values, not parameter limits." :answer/id #uuid "d2001aa0-3c3d-5942-9975-a0c75f0aa7e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{16}\\left(- 2 t\\right)\\,\\left(1+\\left(2 t\\right)^2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "a565f977-b638-5c4e-9f5b-978e41f9e805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-4}^{-1}\\left(- 2 t^{2}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(2 t\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720418} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbaf5422-6537-50fa-9fdb-a0d6aea89b77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720425}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "374a1f06-02d7-56f9-837f-ff1093c427cc" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the section of $y=x^{2}$ with $x<0$ between its intersections with the horizontal lines $y=16$ and $y=1$.\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(- 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nusing $x=t$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "First solve the intersection equations on the specified branch:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x^{2}=16&\\implies x=-4\\\\\nx^{2}=1&\\implies x=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet $x=t$. Parametrize the curve by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,t^{2}\\rangle,\\qquad -4\\le t\\le -1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinates and take the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle 1,2 t\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{1+\\left(2 t\\right)^2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates into the scalar function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=- 2 \\left(t^{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=- 2 t^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the scalar by the speed and use the parameter bounds:\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{-4}^{-1} f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nThus the required setup is\n\n$$\n\\int_{-4}^{-1}\\left(- 2 t^{2}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(2 t\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720409 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "56793fe4-393b-5df6-ba45-f33cb98b2174" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\left(3 t + 1\\right) e^{t}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(3\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720405} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. The speed is a square root of the sum of squared coordinate derivatives. The parameter is $t=x$; horizontal levels are $y$-values, not parameter limits." :answer/id #uuid "83b8585f-9016-5614-9871-b5b0f7a609a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{4}^{7}\\left(e^{t}\\right)\\,\\left(1+\\left(3\\right)^2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720410} {:answer/feedback "The speed is a square root of the sum of squared coordinate derivatives." :answer/id #uuid "9fa949ea-d395-5265-a39b-07000d78a9a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\left(3 t + 1\\right) e^{t}\\right)\\,\\left(1+\\left(3\\right)^2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720416} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation. The speed is a square root of the sum of squared coordinate derivatives. The parameter is $t=x$; horizontal levels are $y$-values, not parameter limits." :answer/id #uuid "a1355398-f8ae-5ef1-afbf-919c6d7a3c5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{4}^{7}\\left(\\left(3 t + 1\\right) e^{3 t + 1}\\right)\\,\\left(1+\\left(3\\right)^2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720417} {:answer/feedback "Substitute both coordinates into the scalar function without dropping a factor or term or changing its operation." :answer/id #uuid "afd1d4ab-d361-5a36-8363-00f813df050b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\left(3 t + 1\\right) e^{3 t + 1}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(3\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "The parameter bounds, scalar substitution and positive arc-length factor all agree." :answer/id #uuid "56793fe4-393b-5df6-ba45-f33cb98b2174" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\left(3 t + 1\\right) e^{t}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(3\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720405} :answer-field/id #uuid "7be61516-1afd-5d93-a18f-76844c49d880" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7cf0ba62-cd75-519f-8d0c-439f967bb847" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the section of $y=3 x + 1$ between its intersections with the horizontal lines $y=4$ and $y=7$.\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(y e^{x}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nusing $x=t$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "First solve the intersection equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 x + 1=4&\\implies x=1\\\\\n3 x + 1=7&\\implies x=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet $x=t$. Parametrize the curve by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,3 t + 1\\rangle,\\qquad 1\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinates and take the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\langle 1,3\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{1+\\left(3\\right)^2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates into the scalar function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf r(t))&=\\left(3 t + 1\\right) e^{t}\\\\\n&=\\left(3 t + 1\\right) e^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply the scalar by the speed and use the parameter bounds:\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s=\\int_{1}^{2} f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nThus the required setup is\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{2}\\left(\\left(3 t + 1\\right) e^{t}\\right)\\,\\sqrt{1+\\left(3\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720486 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2714a5cd-b5d3-5035-94f9-fa805c0391e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720481} {:answer/id #uuid "883e65b2-0606-51b7-9f5d-9c4b911814bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720488} {:answer/id #uuid "990784ef-80ef-572d-8825-4f3997d5a46c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720489} {:answer/id #uuid "99a770b5-f70c-599f-88d5-94d0618f0725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720490} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c153c6-e3e1-56a8-ad88-5ca5b41c16c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "883e65b2-0606-51b7-9f5d-9c4b911814bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720488} :answer-field/id #uuid "6550d90b-5e9d-514c-9eb7-c4b968f97722" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720484}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "780d58a0-41a3-5ec8-bf8e-19895d611a5f" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F=\\ln(x+2y)\\,\\mathbf i+xe^{2y}\\,\\mathbf j.\n$$\n\nEvaluate $\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf F$ at the point $(1,0)$." :question/worked-solution "For $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$, use\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf F=\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial x}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate before evaluating at the point. The other coordinate is held constant in each derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf F\n&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\ln(x+2y)+\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(xe^{2y})\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{x+2y}+2xe^{2y}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe logarithm requires $x+2y>0$, which holds at $(1,0)$. Thus\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf F)(1,0)\n&=\\frac{1}{1+2(0)}+2(1)e^{2(0)}\\\\\n&=1+2\\\\\n&=3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720491 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16c9cec2-2b9b-5dfe-af1e-d1fc0c7423aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^2+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720480} {:answer/id #uuid "743e383e-9297-58ef-9a21-aa1822f132e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^2+\\ln 3+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720485} {:answer/id #uuid "bcca685e-e28d-50b6-914e-cc4c3420b89a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^2+\\ln 3+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720493} {:answer/id #uuid "c9152648-c4f7-5afe-a043-a15e215a267d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^2+\\ln 3+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720496} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c29249-b88f-534d-9d97-c9ee32cdf36d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^2+\\ln 3+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7c29249-b88f-534d-9d97-c9ee32cdf36d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^2+\\ln 3+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720499} :answer-field/id #uuid "37f34123-4091-51b2-9d39-f0353aa32d69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9f4ad0cb-a5bd-5faa-adec-fb3d263b2854" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F=xe^{xy}\\,\\mathbf i+y\\ln(x+y)\\,\\mathbf j.\n$$\n\nEvaluate $\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf F$ at the point $(2,1)$." :question/worked-solution "The divergence is a scalar:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf F=\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial x}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nBoth components require the product rule. In the first derivative, hold $y$ constant and use $\\partial(xy)/\\partial x=y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial x}\n&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(xe^{xy})\\\\\n&=e^{xy}+xye^{xy}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the second derivative, hold $x$ constant and differentiate the logarithm using the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y}\n&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\bigl(y\\ln(x+y)\\bigr)\\\\\n&=\\ln(x+y)+\\frac{y}{x+y}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the derivatives before substituting. Since $2+1>0$, the point lies in the domain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf F\n&=(1+xy)e^{xy}+\\ln(x+y)+\\frac{y}{x+y},\\\\\n(\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf F)(2,1)\n&=(1+2\\cdot1)e^{2\\cdot1}+\\ln(2+1)+\\frac{1}{2+1}\\\\\n&=3e^2+\\ln 3+\\frac{1}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720497 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12a99d52-5c2f-5fa8-ba09-abc3ff68e3c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3y^2\\,\\mathbf i+2x^2\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720479} {:answer/id #uuid "43d24dc4-13af-5acf-b1c6-d714f66413d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^2+3y^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720483} {:answer/id #uuid "7d573d44-3e01-5588-aadb-7f865ba58c85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^2+2y^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720487} {:answer/id #uuid "a4757964-66e2-5ed8-8063-1838b70e34ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720492} {:answer/id #uuid "c37b8528-2da8-59d9-ae89-8e9b6c752e54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6xy\\,\\mathbf i+4xy\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43d24dc4-13af-5acf-b1c6-d714f66413d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^2+3y^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720483} :answer-field/id #uuid "e18befbd-992a-581c-a806-2042cd462aa4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720498}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dcd30809-9b30-57ab-9a4a-be15f9861b2c" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F=3xy^2\\,\\mathbf i+2x^2y\\,\\mathbf j,\n$$\nwhat is $\\operatorname{div}\\mathbf F$?" :question/worked-solution "For a two-dimensional vector field $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$, the divergence is the scalar field\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf F=\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial x}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nTreat $y$ as constant in the first derivative and $x$ as constant in the second:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf F\n&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(3xy^2)+\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(2x^2y)\\\\\n&=3y^2+2x^2\\\\\n&=2x^2+3y^2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a scalar field, so no unit vectors remain."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720811 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cbf0e6a-ddcd-501e-a67a-cd2fa638d0d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720816} {:answer/id #uuid "d0dfc72a-f5c0-5ac8-993e-465c362c6323" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0dfc72a-f5c0-5ac8-993e-465c362c6323" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720852} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd4dc55-10e5-59e5-89b0-bfa02261af26" :answer-field/key "$\\nabla\\cdot F>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720801} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54e28ae0-de0e-54ac-af71-ec86ce27b014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720814} {:answer/id #uuid "91e04eb7-2fb4-5300-b6a8-b6abf109f515" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54e28ae0-de0e-54ac-af71-ec86ce27b014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720814} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cc9e494-c354-5ab6-b644-62359343b35d" :answer-field/key "$F$ is solenoidal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720812} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29c99c3f-4b37-5e6d-93ef-d65fa2880e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720804} {:answer/id #uuid "abb4c517-163c-5d00-97c4-5866a38ee706" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29c99c3f-4b37-5e6d-93ef-d65fa2880e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720804} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ed883df-04f8-5a47-9e17-65acbd2d6254" :answer-field/key "$\\nabla\\cdot F<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720825} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d365d8e-4c8e-5095-8f02-e2d1481d132a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720824} {:answer/id #uuid "ea76424b-e809-58b5-83de-658d7aa5ab7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d365d8e-4c8e-5095-8f02-e2d1481d132a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720824} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3e3c228-9db1-5533-81b5-fcb0b7e15b9b" :answer-field/key "$\\nabla\\cdot F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720854}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "44565916-4b23-55bd-b260-0a83708b9c87" :question/problem "![](images/ef/efd68ffa6f7ef447e6a0a6cc9a982eb44d8ac728e410349f1b9091b52003832e.png)\n\nConsider the smooth vector field $F$ shown above. The displayed pattern continues throughout the plane. All arrows use the same length scale; lengths represent speed. Which statements are true everywhere?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\operatorname{div} F=\\nabla\\cdot F$ denotes divergence. A local excess of outward flow means positive divergence (**source**); inward flow means negative divergence (**sink**); balanced flow means zero divergence.\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nA field is **solenoidal** exactly when its divergence is zero everywhere.\n\nThe $y$-component increases as we move in the positive $y$-direction. The $x$-component is constant, so its flux across opposite sides balances. Thus there is a local excess of outward flow everywhere.\n\nTherefore, $\\nabla\\cdot F>0$ everywhere, and $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nThe true statements are $\\nabla\\cdot F>0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6056933f-560e-5173-8994-b24d5ec86814" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720818} {:answer/id #uuid "78df5696-4a64-5472-92cf-dc5a4d9134bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78df5696-4a64-5472-92cf-dc5a4d9134bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720827} :answer-field/id #uuid "99438bfe-2180-562a-8304-7b4f1b458b5f" :answer-field/key "$F$ is solenoidal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720833} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63c29daf-c37d-5a0d-af3b-2419f1ea8609" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720822} {:answer/id #uuid "8fc40344-7067-58e7-b12e-50ba2b76e284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63c29daf-c37d-5a0d-af3b-2419f1ea8609" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720822} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9e191f1-6a1a-52b2-a8f6-2dc74aeef093" :answer-field/key "$\\nabla\\cdot F>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720838} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0733ef9c-2313-576f-bf7f-5d0a21bc444f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720797} {:answer/id #uuid "bc9a03c0-371c-57f7-9742-cacd21d4e88e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0733ef9c-2313-576f-bf7f-5d0a21bc444f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720797} :answer-field/id #uuid "caea7375-2581-5e4b-a762-b4e0cf926b8a" :answer-field/key "$\\nabla\\cdot F<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720849} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acb65b05-46c9-56af-94cc-acf8453b27f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720842} {:answer/id #uuid "b2318dbe-209a-5244-aceb-580d7f44b19b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acb65b05-46c9-56af-94cc-acf8453b27f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720842} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7223bc1-abfa-5ad6-bc50-a6631e5b850d" :answer-field/key "$\\nabla\\cdot F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720856}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "61c14c15-1de3-51a9-97b1-df61e0b67ef5" :question/problem "![](images/80/802493db8a1ee96693f3b5bc5a5183202021dd5f7348e8b175081eb1958e4beb.png)\n\nConsider the smooth vector field $F$ shown above. The displayed pattern continues throughout the plane. All arrows use the same length scale; lengths represent speed. Which statements are true everywhere?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\operatorname{div} F=\\nabla\\cdot F$ denotes divergence. A local excess of outward flow means positive divergence (**source**); inward flow means negative divergence (**sink**); balanced flow means zero divergence.\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nA field is **solenoidal** exactly when its divergence is zero everywhere.\n\nThe $y$-component decreases as we move in the positive $y$-direction. The $x$-component is constant, so its flux across opposite sides balances. Thus there is a local excess of inward flow everywhere.\n\nTherefore, $\\nabla\\cdot F<0$ everywhere, and $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nThe true statements are $\\nabla\\cdot F<0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d9756cc-124c-55fa-8d0d-3eefa51f46a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720829} {:answer/id #uuid "dc8124f0-5875-5013-9382-bce7a636dcc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d9756cc-124c-55fa-8d0d-3eefa51f46a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720829} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ef1747a-ab6d-5ba8-962b-1e9b18a5b161" :answer-field/key "$\\nabla\\cdot F>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720798} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "402f232a-a6cd-59f0-9a84-07724c2dd664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720810} {:answer/id #uuid "721caf4e-67f4-5a5b-bfb6-3a8f0b95ffc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "721caf4e-67f4-5a5b-bfb6-3a8f0b95ffc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720826} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dd9aed7-5a28-588d-b893-b75b00637126" :answer-field/key "$\\nabla\\cdot F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720807} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f789052-ec26-5a26-9dec-c58ee540cb91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720802} {:answer/id #uuid "a6efa148-c9ff-5030-abb2-74350cb10a48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6efa148-c9ff-5030-abb2-74350cb10a48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720836} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa613a3b-aeec-59ec-9f98-ab5f21ab5e18" :answer-field/key "$\\nabla\\cdot F<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720839} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a64b9bc-3731-5a71-8bbb-52a800d2487d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720823} {:answer/id #uuid "8e9eba10-a61d-5d98-affd-1f20df42a306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e9eba10-a61d-5d98-affd-1f20df42a306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720830} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab633f92-1209-5923-bc9d-14d653f047f9" :answer-field/key "$F$ is solenoidal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "632e721f-bde9-59ea-940d-18de3c8e6cfa" :question/problem "![](images/5b/5be0abcb12fdda5266a437299cc76978ba0c154c330ca4089750fde877462408.png)\n\nConsider the smooth vector field $F$ shown above. The displayed pattern continues throughout the plane. All arrows use the same length scale; lengths represent speed. Which statements are true everywhere?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\operatorname{div} F=\\nabla\\cdot F$ denotes divergence. A local excess of outward flow means positive divergence (**source**); inward flow means negative divergence (**sink**); balanced flow means zero divergence.\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nA field is **solenoidal** exactly when its divergence is zero everywhere.\n\nThe $x$-component changes only as we move in the $y$-direction. At a fixed $y$-coordinate, opposite sides normal to the $x$-axis have matching components. The $y$-component is constant as well. All normal fluxes across opposite sides balance, even though arrow lengths vary.\n\nTherefore, $\\nabla\\cdot F=0$ everywhere, and $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nThe true statements are $\\nabla\\cdot F=0$ and $F$ is solenoidal."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720846 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1886c3de-df23-5d65-bcab-e4e20240cefd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720799} {:answer/id #uuid "d0845dd2-5a7c-5de6-9716-e9122b1bcbd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1886c3de-df23-5d65-bcab-e4e20240cefd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720799} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f6d5556-aceb-5d4a-96ba-8001f701a008" :answer-field/key "$\\nabla\\cdot F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720809} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb907e8d-b37f-5cdf-a353-593572e9a565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720860} {:answer/id #uuid "f0386f8d-e4f4-5bae-8f31-ab33f1f484bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb907e8d-b37f-5cdf-a353-593572e9a565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720860} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a5ac29f-9b07-508c-9030-9cc37c00555b" :answer-field/key "$\\nabla\\cdot F<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720828} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3972cc22-3d29-592f-87f3-26963af50264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720805} {:answer/id #uuid "57d48d3f-3443-50ff-a4fd-9f979bc61521" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3972cc22-3d